patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111562.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"- Motivated by and prepares for #106873 \r\n\r\nVarious servers are currently being created and registered earlier than needed. Especially, they're created before being registered, and before related types being registered. This could lead to subtle bugs, and defies with expected initialization order.\r\nThis PR rectifies this, by moving singleton registrations of 3 servers into the expected location, and by registering core types and singletons before server types and singletons.\r\n\r\nI tested the launcher, tests, and the editor, and I'm seeing no regressions. I can't discern any particular reasons why the order was the way it was before, instead of the 'expected' way (core before servers, types before singletons).\r\n\r\nI'm not super happy with having to take any 'risks' to fix initialization order, but I'm guessing the initialization order never getting a hard look is how it ended up being this messy. I'm open to ideas, but personally I think we might just have to take it in tiny steps that look safe and hope for the best.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111562/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111562/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}